term:
While the comprehensive theory of Pathos Particles was first proposed by Carlson, the Particles themselves had already been around for millions of years.
Pathos Particles are fundamental, naturally occurring particles generated primarily by intelligent, living organisms through emotional and cognitive activities. However, all things do generate Pathos Particles. In particular, when a living organism is immersed in an emotion, this triggers the production of a significant quantity of corresponding Pathos Particles, unleashing a powerful force of Pathos Energy.
When P-values reach a certain level, they can be observed directly by Felinians. Humans can observe them indirectly through use of specialized devices. When observed, these particles emit different colors; these variations are caused by the proportions of internal particles in each blend.

Types of Pathos Particles:
Red: Represents Anger;
Green: Represents Joy;
Blue: Represents Sadness;
White : This special Pathos Particle represents positive emotions and appears yellow-white;
Black: This special Pathos Particle represents negative emotions, and appears dark purple.
